The node app runs on 127.0.0.1:1337 and I am listening to mydomain:8080 and forward it.
Unfortunately it gives my a 502 bad gateway when I turn off the node app and request mydomain:8080 .
This is the expected behaviour from nginx though. What I want is a page I can define that w

Log/Config:
server {
listen 8080;
server_name mydomain;
access_log /log/path/logging.log;
root /path/to/root/;
error_page 400 401 402 403 404 500 501 502 503 504 /error/index.html;
location / {
